![](termux-nix.jpg)

[termux-nix](https://github.com/aca/termux-nix): an Android X11 desktop configured with nix.

Lately, I've been having fun with termux and termux-x11. Carrying a laptop all the time is a hassle,
and I have always wanted to build a cyberdeck. But SoC-based devices often have hardware quality issues,
so I ended up with termux / termux-x11 on Android.

I worked outside with this setup for more than 30 minutes, and I'm quite happy with the result.
I tried [nix-on-droid](https://github.com/nix-community/nix-on-droid),
but chose native termux because of the proot overhead. So I made a project called [termux-nix](https://github.com/aca/termux-nix):

- builds nix derivations outside Android, because building inside proot crashes randomly
- rsyncs the result to termux and runs scripts, similar to home-manager
- runs nix applications inside a proot container that shares /tmp, storage, etc. with termux

"Happy Hacking!" 
